<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2d4b56bcfba9a94395af5896f274ebade9e39081" commit="ae39485a7fc90f353736fcf6976c30034e9ec1b8" commit_message="cgpt: Fully write out primary GPT before starting to write secondary  The point of having two GPTs is to always have a known good one if one of them gets corrupted. One of the most obvious ways that could happen is if the write stopped half-way through (e.g. due to a crash or random power loss).  Unfortunately, the way we currently save modified GPTs can leave both copies invalid if we stop writing at just the wrong time. Since a GPT header contains a checksum over the GPT entries, we need to write both the header and entries for one GPT (and make sure they're synced to disk) before we start writing the other.  BRANCH=None BUG=chrome-os-partner:52595 TEST=None  Change-Id: I2d4b56bcfba9a94395af5896f274ebade9e39081 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340071 Reviewed-by: Nam Nguyen &lt;namnguyen@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="340071" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/71/340071/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7e53542385ae9d8d24dc25b75e91f4ff4917f66f" commit="a847b2a62ae4a47747ae2b97f1dc3f76b9c09bf5" commit_message="cgptlib: Add support for IGNOREME GPT signature  This patch makes cgpt aware of a special &quot;IGNOREME&quot; GPT header signature string that may appear in either the primary or the secondary GPT and cause cgpt (and other cgptlib clients) to completely ignore that GPT. It will continue to function correctly for all other purposes (using the data from the non-ignored GPT), but never write any data back to the ignored GPT.  BRANCH=None BUG=chrome-os-partner:52595 TEST=unit tests  Change-Id: I7e53542385ae9d8d24dc25b75e91f4ff4917f66f Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340072 Reviewed-by: Nam Nguyen &lt;namnguyen@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="340072" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/72/340072/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If2835fec28a9c39373abd050e2e057f73e5ec700" commit="443cd3fb70ff0871a5704163d1aeb70fb5c8d708" commit_message="cgpt: Add cgpt legacy parameter to set primary GPT signature to IGNOREME  Now that we have support for the IGNOREME signature in cgpt, we need a way to set it on an existing disk. The easiest option is to shoehorn this into the cgpt legacy command, because that's already made to modify GPT header signatures (really, it would be nice to rename it to cgpt signature or something, but let's not break existing uses for now).  BRANCH=None BUG=chrome-os-partner:52595 TEST=unit tests  Change-Id: If2835fec28a9c39373abd050e2e057f73e5ec700 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340073 Reviewed-by: Nam Nguyen &lt;namnguyen@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="340073" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/73/340073/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3fd88ae3cca32702f8b537f673d6db2941e3e7f7" commit="37cc60bdc9a64d77ee955277edf85fadff802712" commit_message="[autotest] Update LabelRetriever to create labels everywhere.  This change does one major thing: 1. Update the rpc_interface host_add_labels() to create labels    if they don't exist on the master first, then to the shards.  With these changes, we should be creating labels on the master AFE and propagating those changes to the shards properly.  BUG=chromium:603420 TEST=Locally on moblab and on test server with shard, verified label gets created on test server and shard with same label ids.  Also all unittests pass.  Change-Id: I3fd88ae3cca32702f8b537f673d6db2941e3e7f7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/338904 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="338904" owner_email="kevcheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/04/338904/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I92d395bdace78f791dbd58cbb59a5a4df283da0c" commit="bbf166457052f2cce4983cc133a284b3c3b3da60" commit_message="ANDROID: net: wireless: bcmdhd: Remove ePNO support bit  &quot;Remove the ePNO support bit in capabilities since Nexus 6 will not support the new ePNO in Android N.&quot;  We do the same for Ryu because it's ePNO implementation is not compatible with N and it is not actually used in M.  BUG=b:27681768 BUG=b:28257814 TEST=Boot ryu, switch airplane mode on and off, verify wifi reconnects  Change-Id: I92d395bdace78f791dbd58cbb59a5a4df283da0c Signed-off-by: Ashwin &lt;ashwin.bhat@broadcom.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340494 Reviewed-by: Sameer Nanda &lt;snanda@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Roshan Pius &lt;rpius@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="340494" owner_email="dtor@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/94/340494/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I815dbd85f113f25e5f1a0cbd3117466e23d2cf1d" commit="55562f09f807c4d64343dad33565532cd52d5996" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau: Don't reference vma after unmap  In nouveau_gem_ioctl_unmap(), after the call to nouveau_gem_object_unmap(), assume that the vma can be freed at any point after that, and avoid further references to the vma.  The only other reference to the vma after this point is a peek at the as to see if the address space allocation is sparse, so save off as before calling nouveau_gem_object_unmap().  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52570 TEST=Build and boot to desktop on A44.  Change-Id: I815dbd85f113f25e5f1a0cbd3117466e23d2cf1d Signed-off-by: Andrew Chew &lt;achew@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340333 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="340333" owner_email="achew@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/33/340333/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1e8a759e5bfdea44eb92f1d9e10d684a361d8c34" commit="ef4c1d73bda1ec9452598942f206f9389e68e911" commit_message="Add veyron_fievel to builder configuration  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I1e8a759e5bfdea44eb92f1d9e10d684a361d8c34 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340444 Commit-Ready: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="340444" owner_email="philipchen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chro